# Stack

- Monorepo: Turborepo + Bun
- apps/web: Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui
- packages/db: Drizzle ORM schema, Supabase Postgres
- packages/mcp-orchestrator: MCP client wiring for Claude tool use
- Auth: Supabase Auth (magic link, no passwords)
- Storage: Supabase Storage
- Hosting: Vercel
- AI: Anthropic Claude API. BYOK per user — each user stores their own
  encrypted Anthropic API key. Never use Claude.ai subscription/OAuth
  tokens for this; that is not permitted by Anthropic outside Claude Code
  and Claude.ai itself.

# Core domain model

- Everything is scoped to a `workspace_id`: workspaces → workspace_members
  (role: owner/member/viewer) → projects → tasks → time_entries
- A user can belong to multiple workspaces (fully separate contexts,
  not just a filter on the same data)
- chat_threads, chat_messages, notifications, integrations, and
  pending_actions are also scoped to workspace_id
- pending_actions represents AI-proposed write actions (e.g. "reply to
  customer", "update project status") that require explicit user
  confirmation before execution — never execute a write action from the
  AI chat without going through this table first

# Conventions

- TypeScript strict mode, no `any`
- Server Actions / API routes for all mutations — never write to Supabase
  directly from client components
- Prefer the Drizzle query builder over raw SQL, except where a Row Level
  Security policy requires SQL directly in a migration
- Log every mutation to `activity_log` (workspace_id, user_id,
  entity_type, entity_id, action, created_at) — this doubles as the
  Activity feed and the audit trail for AI-initiated actions
